<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Proportional shares from one share</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Three farmers, {@nA@}, {@nB@} and {@nC@}, paid Ksh \({@ksh(cx)@}\), Ksh \({@ksh(cy)@}\) and Ksh \({@ksh(cz)@}\) to hire a tractor. They shared the money from their harvest in proportion to what each paid. {@nA@} received Ksh \({@ksh(R)@}\).</p><p>(a) How much money was shared altogether?</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) How much did {@nC@} receive?</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Sharing in proportion to what each paid means sharing in the ratio of the payments:</p><p>\({@ksh(cx)@} : {@ksh(cy)@} : {@ksh(cz)@} = {@px@} : {@py@} : {@pz@}\), which is \({@pS@}\) parts in all.</p><p>(a) {@nA@}'s \({@px@}\) parts are Ksh \({@ksh(R)@}\), so one part is \({@ksh(R)@} \div {@px@} = {@ksh(one)@}\). The total is \({@pS@} \times {@ksh(one)@} = {@ksh(Tt)@}\), so Ksh \({@ksh(Tt)@}\) was shared.</p><p>(b) {@nC@} receives \({@pz@} \times {@ksh(one)@} = {@ksh(C)@}\), so Ksh \({@ksh(C)@}\).</p><p>Check: {@nB@} receives \({@py@} \times {@ksh(one)@} = {@ksh(py*one)@}\), and \({@ksh(R)@} + {@ksh(py*one)@} + {@ksh(C)@} = {@ksh(Tt)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
fr(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else sconcat("\\frac{", string(num(v)), "}{", string(denom(v)), "}");
r1(v) := floor(10*v+1/2)/10;
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: find shares in proportion from one known share. Source: original. [cx, cy, cz, R]: what A, B, C paid, and A's share. Curated list, one seed per entry. */
L: [[18000,24000,42000,9600],[20000,45000,35000,12000],[10000,16000,22000,7500],[25000,30000,55000,10000],[6000,15000,27000,5400],[35000,20000,45000,17500],[40000,28000,56000,20000],[48000,30000,42000,25600],[9000,33000,18000,6300],[50000,15000,35000,37500]];
E: L[ix];
cx: E[1]; cy: E[2]; cz: E[3]; R: E[4];
nms: ["Akinyi","Kiprop","Wambui","Otieno","Nafula","Mwangi","Jepkosgei","Wekesa","Nyokabi","Abdi"];
nA: nms[ix]; nB: nms[mod(ix+2,10)+1]; nC: nms[mod(ix+5,10)+1];
S: cx+cy+cz;
g: gcd(gcd(cx,cy),cz);
px: cx/g; py: cy/g; pz: cz/g; pS: px+py+pz;
one: R/px;
Tt: R*S/cx;
C: R*cz/cx;
/* diagnostics */
eq3: 3*R;
oth: R*(cy+cz)/cx;
inv: R*cx/cz;
reh: (Tt-R)/2;
cmpw: if cx<min(cy,cz) then "paid less than each of the others" else if cx>max(cy,cz) then "paid more than each of the others" else "paid a different amount from each of the others";
zmore: if cz>cx then "more" else "less";
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
